learned.projects/fixture-hybrid-r0-ac95b45a/PLAY:
[
  {
    "id": "p1",
    "text": "Run the full suite with `make test` (it runs `PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`); `./tools/test` does not exist — tools/ holds only `checksum` and `gen-fixtures` — and a bare `python3 -m unittest` fails to import `tally` (src layout).",
    "helpful": 7,
    "harmful": 1
  },
  {
    "id": "p2",
    "text": "Tests need fixtures generated first: run `./tools/gen-fixtures --seed 59cf83ccafd7` (the team seed) so `.fixtures/golden.json` exists; it's gitignored and `tests/test_ledger.py` asserts its `seed_check` hash.",
    "helpful": 8,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p3",
    "text": "If a fixture/test file is missing or its expected hash doesn't match, ask the user for the value (e.g. the team seed) instead of brute-forcing the hash or committing a hand-made fixture.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p4",
    "text": "Nothing is pushed and no remote is configured in this repo; the release ends with the local commit and annotated tag.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p5",
    "text": "For cut a tally release: version bump, changelog move, checksum artifact, one commit, annotated tag: load the `tally-release` skill first and follow its steps.",
    "helpful": 1,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p6",
    "text": "New subcommands: add `sub.add_parser(...)` in `build_parser()` and a matching `elif args.cmd == \"...\"` in `main()` in src/tally/cli.py, but keep the computation out of cli.py as a function returning lines of text — report.py for reports, a separate module (e.g. sync.py) for commands that hit the network — the CLI only prints them.",
    "helpful": 4,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p7",
    "text": "Validate CLI argument values in a `type=` callable that raises `argparse.ArgumentTypeError` (e.g. `_month` for YYYY-MM built via `date.fromisoformat(f\"{text}-01\")`), so bad input exits 2 with the usage message.",
    "helpful": 3,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p8",
    "text": "Amounts are `Decimal` everywhere (src/tally/money.py): use `Decimal(\"0\")` as a zero default/fallback in report and CLI code — `money.quantize(0)` with an int arg raises, and comparing a total against a limit needs both sides Decimal.",
    "helpful": 2,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p9",
    "text": "Every change, bug fix included, gets a line under the `## Unreleased` heading in CHANGELOG.md (above the latest released `## X.Y.Z` section) — don't leave it for release time.",
    "helpful": 2,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p10",
    "text": "Command code that talks to the outside world (e.g. the POST client) goes in its own module (src/tally/sync.py with `config()`, `payload()`, `push()`), not in cli.py; tests patch it as `tally.sync.urllib.request.urlopen`.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p11",
    "text": "Never put the staging token in a file, test, README, or shell command: tests must mock `urllib.request.urlopen` (no network) and use a dummy token, and manual checks go against a local `http.server` with `TALLY_TOKEN=abc`.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p12",
    "text": "Shell writes outside the repo fail here (`cat > /tmp/x.py` → Permission denied); create throwaway scripts inside the repo (e.g. `.srv.py`) and delete them before finishing.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  }
]
